 Or another example if your position adjustment assumes it can do 1 additional buy with 3x the original stake amount then `custom_stake_amount` should return 25% of proposed stake amount and leave 75% for possible later position adjustments.
 
+#### Limiting exposure to a single currency
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against, or backed by, the same underlying currency (for example several USDT-margined futures, or several coins quoted against the same stablecoin), a large adverse move in that one currency can hit multiple open trades at once - even though each trade looked fine in isolation.
+
+`max_single_currency_exposure` limits the combined stake committed to all simultaneously open trades that share the same underlying (base) currency, as a fraction of the total tradable capital (as returned by [`tradable_balance_ratio`](#tradable-balance) / [`available_capital`](#assign-available-capital)).
+
+For example, with a total tradable capital of 1000 USDT and `max_single_currency_exposure=0.3`, no more than 300 USDT may be committed at once to open trades whose pair base currency is `BTC` - regardless of how many separate `BTC/...` pairs are involved, or how much of the 300 USDT any single one of those trades uses.
+
+When opening (or increasing) a trade would push the combined exposure to its base currency above the configured limit, the stake amount is reduced to fit under the limit, the same way it's reduced when it would otherwise exceed the available balance or the exchange's maximum stake. If the resulting stake would fall below the minimum tradable amount for the pair, the trade is skipped entirely, exactly as with any other stake amount that ends up too small. This applies identically in live/dry-run and in backtesting.
+
+!!! Note
+    This setting is disabled by default (no limit applied). It's evaluated per pair's base currency - e.g. `BTC/USDT` and `ETH/USDT` are treated as different currencies, while `BTC/USDT` and `BTC/USDC` (if both traded) would be treated as the same underlying currency.
+
